seed.push({id:'DEV-063',title:'Transaction timestamps and member submission deadlines',area:'Contributions',kind:'Task',status:'Ready to test',priority:'High',release:'MVP',owner:'',due:'',dependencies:'DEV-050, DEV-058, DEV-060',description:'Display server recording timestamps with seconds and time zone. Capture per-member obligation cutoff date/time/zone and the cutoff that applied when a contribution was submitted; show on-time or late submission separately from receipt verification.',criteria:'New manual and weekly obligations require a cutoff.\nOwner can record or correct individual cutoffs with history and stale-version protection.\nSubmissions at the cutoff are on time; client clocks and backdated payment dates cannot alter server recording time.\nChanged cutoffs preserve earlier submission snapshots.\nLegacy missing cutoffs are explicit and are never inferred.\nDST gaps/overlaps are rejected.\nStanding, Activity, statements and CSV agree on exact overdue time.\nNo fees are applied.',notes:'2026-10-01: Implemented timestamps, manual/weekly cutoffs, history, immutable submission snapshots, comparison labels, and CSV fields. Five focused deadline scenarios, eight existing API pilot scenarios, funding/policy/governance/statement regressions and TypeScript passed. Read-only audit: 102 entries have recording times; 99 obligations have no cutoffs. No live cutoffs were set. Browser/mobile and real-member acceptance remain pending.',version:1,updated:'2026-10-01T17:00:00.000Z'});
